# Given: a server with no keyring, the component installed, and the fixture key
# When: the key-argument functions are used
1	1
# Then: they work exactly as on any other server (above)
# Scenario 2 — Given: the same server
# When: each key-id function is called
# Then: each reports that the keyring is unavailable (errors section)
# Scenario 3 — Given: gcm.strict turned OFF, in a new connection so it applies on every major
# When: a key-id function is called
# Then: still an error, not NULL — a missing keyring is not hidden by the setting (errors section)
# Scenario 4 — Given: a NULL key id
# When: a key-id function is called
1
# Then: NULL, with no error — the keyring is not consulted (above)
# Scenario 5 — Given: the same server, with no keyring
# When: the usage of a key id is read
[0, 0, true]
# Then: zeros — gcm_key_usage reads the component's own table and needs no keyring (above)
